Originally titled "Asylum", the film becomes a journey
into Poitras's disillusionment with Assange.

13
01:13:56,250 --> 01:14:02,250
In the 2016 version of the film, Poitras presents a more
sympathetic position towards Assange.

14
01:19:37,500 --> 01:19:43,500
The 2017 re-cut version focuses more on a critique of Assange as a flawed character, including his alleged
sexual assaults and his "troubling" statements about women and responses to accusations against him.

